n a plate with 4 Bowl arrange Turmeric, kumkum, Sandal Powder and Akshatha (uncooked rice mixed with turmeric in a small cup)(add 2 drops of ghee for mixing well)</li>\r\n<li>arrange all fruits in a plate or foils trays.</li>\r\n<li>Cut all Flowers and arrange in a plate or foils trays</li>\r\n<li>Keep all other puja samagri around it.</li>\r\n<li>Before starting the Pooja the host couple should wear dresses suitable and appropriate for the Pooja as per the family tradition. Typically the husband should wear Indian silk Dhoti and the silk kurta or regular Kurta Pajama. Wife of the host should wear a sari or salwar kamiz dupatta etc</li>\r\n</ol>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,22,'2025-02-01 10:37:30','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(66,'Hiranyashrardam','hiranyashrardam','15','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<div class=\"responsive-table text-center\">\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">Things Needed For Puja at The Temple</h3>\r\n<table class=\"custom-table\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>S.no</th>\r\n<th>Item Name</th>\r\n<th>Quantity</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n<td>Flowers Bouquet</td>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>2</td>\r\n<td>Betel Leaves and Nuts (Pan, Supari)</td>\r\n<td>Minimum 5</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>3</td>\r\n<td>Uncooked Rice</td>\r\n<td>-</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>4</td>\r\n<td>Moong or Toor Dal</td>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>5</td>\r\n<td>Black Sesame Seeds</td>\r\n<td>-</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>6</td>\r\n<td>Coins</td>\r\n<td>-</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>7</td>\r\n<td>Fruits</td>\r\n<td>-</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>8</td>\r\n<td>Vegetables</td>\r\n<td>5 Types</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>9</td>\r\n<td>Rice Flour or Cooked Rice</td>\r\n<td>1 Pack or 1 Cup</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30 text-center\">Temple Donation</h3>\r\n<h4 class=\" text-center\">Puja at temple - $75/-</h4>\r\n<h5 class=\" text-center\">*Priest dakshina separate for both</h