i around it.</li>\r\n<li>Before starting the Pooja, the host couple should wear dresses suitable and appropriate for the Pooja as per the family tradition. Typically, the husband should wear an Indian silk Dhoti and a silk Kurta or regular Kurta Pajama. The wife of the host should wear a sari or salwar kameez with a dupatta, etc.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"responsive-table text-center\">\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">Navagraha Homam - Things Needed For Puja at the Temple</h3>\r\n<table class=\"custom-table\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>S.no</th>\r\n<th>Item Name</th>\r\n<th>Quantity</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n<td>Turmeric Powder &amp; Kumkum (Gopuram Company)</td>\r\n<td>25 grams</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>2</td>\r\n<td>Camphor</td>\r\n<td>1 Packet</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>3</td>\r\n<td>Coconut</td>\r\n<td>3 Nos</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>4</td>\r\n<td>Rice</td>\r\n<td>3 lbs</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>5</td>\r\n<td>Some Coins</td>\r\n<td>$10 + some cash</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>6</td>\r\n<td>Betel Leaves</td>\r\n<td>20 Nos</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>7</td>\r\n<td>Betel Nuts</td>\r\n<td>15 Nos</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>8</td>\r\n<td>Navadhanyam</td>\r\n<td>Available in Indian Stores</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>9</td>\r\n<td>Flowers (Rose, Carnations, Mums)</td>\r\n<td>3 Bunches</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>10</td>\r\n<td>Fruits (Banana, Pomegranate, etc.)</td>\r\n<td>5 Types - 5 Each</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>11</td>\r\n<td>God Idol (Lakshmi &amp; Ganapati)</td>\r\n<td>-</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>12</td>\r\n<td>Ghee</td>\r\n<td>2 lbs</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>13</td>\r\n<td>Raisins, Cashew, Dates &amp; Almonds</td>\r\n<td>-</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>14</td>\r\n<td>Blouse Piece (Silk)</td>\r\n<td>2.5 Meters</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>15</td>\r\n<td>Havan Samagiri</td>\r\n<td>1 Packet</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>16</td>\r\n<td>Dry Coconut</td>\r\n<td>3 Nos</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>17</td>