yana Picture (not very small one)</td>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>7</td>\r\n<td>Aluminium foils and trays</td>\r\n<td>6 nos</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2 style=\"margin: 20px;\">&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30 text-center\">Temple Donation</h3>\r\n<h4 class=\"text-center\" style=\"margin: 20px;\">&nbsp;Puja at home - $151/-</h4>\r\n<h5 class=\"text-center\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; *Priest dakshina separate for both</h5>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30 text-center\">Arrangement for Sri Satyanarayana puja</h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6\"><img src=\"https://htnadmin.cloudhostingcompany.in/images/media/Screenshot-2025-02-12-165848_30cftmpve.png\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6\"><img src=\"https://htnadmin.cloudhostingcompany.in/images/media/Screenshot-2025-02-12-165854_6hs1rmhrl.png\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Keep a puja stool on the east wall and arrange puja samagri on the right or left side.</li>\r\n<li>In a plate with 4 bowls, arrange Turmeric, Kumkum, Sandal Powder, and Akshatha (uncooked rice mixed with turmeric in a small cup) (add 2 drops of ghee for mixing well).</li>\r\n<li>Arrange all fruits in a plate or foil trays.</li>\r\n<li>Cut all flowers and arrange them in a plate or foil trays.</li>\r\n<li>Mix Panchaamritham with milk, yogurt, sugar, honey, and ghee in a small cup&mdash;prepared fresh on the puja day.</li>\r\n<li>Arrange 4 lamps with cotton wick &amp; oil or ghee.</li>\r\n<li>Before starting the puja, the host couple should wear dresses suitable and appropriate for the puja as per the family tradition. Typically, the husband should wear an Indian silk dhoti and a silk kurta or regular kurta pajama. The wife of the host should wear a sari or salwar kameez with a dupatta, etc.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30 text-center\">Things needed for Puja at the temple</h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<table class=\"custom-table\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>S.no</th>\r\n<th>Item Name</th>\r\n<th>Quantity</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n<td>Turmeric and Kumkum</td>\r\n<td>1 pack</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>2</td>\r\n<td>Fruits (apples, oranges, etc.)</td>\r\n<td>5 varieties - 5 each</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>3</td>\r\n<td>Coconuts (with water)</td>\r\n<td>7</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>4</td>\r\n<td>Prasad Kesari (made of sooji) and any other dish (no onion/garlic)</td>\r\n<td>Prepared fresh on puja day</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>5</td>\r\n<td>Panchaamritham (mix of milk, yogurt, sugar, honey, and ghee)</td>\r\n<td>Small cup - prepared fresh on puja day</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>6</td>\r\n<td>Nava Dhaanyam (available in a packet in Indian stores)</td>\r\n<td>1 packet</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>7</td>\r\n<td>Betel Leaves</td>\r\n<td>25</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>8</td>\r\n<td>Betel Nuts</td>\r\n<td>25 (small quantity)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>9</td>\r\n<td>New blouse piece / Kitchen Hand Towel (for offering to Lord)</td>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>10</td>\r\n<td>Kitchen Hand Towels</td>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>11</td>\r\n<td>Rice (uncooked)</td>\r\n<td>2 lbs</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>12</td>\r\n<td>Coins (25 cent for $10 and $1 cash)</td>\r\n<td>5</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>13</td>\r\n<td>Flowers (roses, carnation, or mums)</td>\r\n<td>4 bunches</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>14</td>\r\n<td>Mango Leaves</td>\r\n<td>1 bunch</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2 style=\"margin: 20px;\">&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30 text-center\">Temple Donation</h3>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-center\" style=\"margin: 20px;\">&nbsp;Puja at temple - $101/-</h3>\r\n<h5 class=\"text-center\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; *Priest dakshina separate for both</h5>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,31,'2025-02-01 10:43:45','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(74,'Shshtipoorthi (60th Birthday)','shshtipoorthi-60th-birthday','15','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">List of Item for Shshtipoorthi (60th Birthday)</h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Picture / Idol of Lord Ganesha</li>\r\n<li>Picture / Idol of Lord Satyanarayana Swamy</li>\r\n<li>Turmeric - One packet each *</li>\r\n<li>Kumkum Powder - One packet each *</li>\r\n<li>Sandal-Wood Paste - Little {if available} *</li>\r\n<li>Akshta (raw rice smeared with turmeric powder and ghee) - in small bowl *</li>\r\n<li>Incense Sticks - One(1) packet *</li>\r\n<li>Camphor - Little</li>\r\n<li>Oil Lamp Stands - Two(2)</li>\r\n<li>A Small Lamp - One(1) [for Aarathi]</li>\r\n<li>Oil or Ghee [for Holy Lamp] *</li>\r\n<li>Cotton Wicks [for Holy Lamp]</li>\r\n<li>Flowers - One Or Two Bunches *</li>\r\n<li>Fruits - Five(5) different kinds *</li>\r\n<li>Betel Leaves - 20 number *</li>\r\n<li>Betel Nuts - 20 number and dry dates *</li>\r\n<li>Coconuts - Two ([One for Kalasa, One for Lord] and also if preferred, can offer additional Five [one per chapter for five chapters in story])</li>\r\n<li>Pooja Mandapam - One(1) {if available}</li>\r\n<li>A small vessel to keep coconut - One(1) [for Kalasa/Kumbha]</li>\r\n<li>Matchbox - One (1)</li>\r\n<li>Bell - One(1) {if available}</li>\r\n<li>One towel and blouse piece [for Kalasa vastra] *</li>\r\n<li>Panchamrutham (Milk, Curd/Yogurt, Ghee, Honey and Sugar) *</li>\r\n<li>Naivedya Or Prasad - (Kesari Type or any traditional Sweet-Pudding, preferably prepared with Sooji, Sugar, Ghee, Milk, Dry Fruits)</li>\r\n<li>Mango Leaves - few bunches {if available} *</li>\r\n<li>Rice - 1 pound *</li>\r\n<li>Plates, Vessels, Spoons [for pooja needs]</li>\r\n<li>Paper Towel/Kitchen Napkins [for pooja needs] *</li>\r\n<li>Scissors [to cut flowers and any packets]</li>\r\n<li>Scotch Tape [if necessary to aid decoration/alankar]</li>\r\n<li>Paper Bowls - Nine(9) [for Navadhanyas]</li>\r\n<li>Navadhanyas (Wheat, Rice, Redgram, Greengram, Black Gram, Bengal Gram, Blackeyedpeas, Sesameseeds, Horse Gram. All these grains are available in any Indian store. Small packets are sufficient. Please arrange each kind of dhanya in a paper bowl before Priest arrives)</li>\r\n<li>Coins -12</li>\r\n<li>Priest dakshina</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>NOTE:</strong> if you are doing pooja in the temple you don&rsquo;t have to bring kalasam, mandapam, oil lamps, match box, incense sticks, lords photos.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">Temple Donation</h3>\r\n<h4>Puja at Temple - $201/-</h4>\r\n<h5>*Priest dakshina separate for both</h5>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">Temple Donation</h3>\r\n<h4>Puja at Home - $251/-</h4>\r\n<h5>*Priest dakshina separate for both</h5>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,30,'2025-02-01 10:44:17','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(75,'Third Sunday Puja','third-sunday-puja','15','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">List of Items for Third Sunday Puja</h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Please contact Panditji and/or Manager to schedule a puja</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Turmeric (Haldi Powder) (Ganesh, Shiva Kritikai don&rsquo;t need)</li>\r\n<li>KumKum (Ganesh, Shiva Kritikai don&rsquo;t need) 1&ndash;2 tsp</li>\r\n<li>Sandal Paste (Chandan) 1 tsp</li>\r\n<li>Fresh Flowers Minimum 1 bouquet</li>\r\n<li>Betel leaves and nuts (Pan, Supari) Minimum 5</li>\r\n<li>Milk 1 gallon</li>\r\n<li>Home or Store Yogurt (mix with water or milk and grind) Minimum &frac12; gallon</li>\r\n<li>Ghee (Purified Butter) 5 tsp</li>\r\n<li>Sugarcane Juice Minimum 1 can</li>\r\n<li>Honey 5 tsp</li>\r\n<li>Orange Juice &frac12; gallon</li>\r\n<li>Coconut water can Minimum 1 can</li>\r\n<li>Vastram (Clothes for God) Optional</li>\r\n<li>Bananas Minimum 5 bananas</li>\r\n<li>Oranges Minimum 5 oranges</li>\r\n<li>Apples Minimum 5 apples</li>\r\n<li>Mangoes (if available) Minimum 5 mangoes</li>\r\n<li>Grapes 1 pound</li>\r\n<li>Pears Minimum 5 pears</li>\r\n<li>More fruits (Your choice)</li>\r\n<li>Coconut 1</li>\r\n<li>Home cooked Prasadam to serve 15&ndash;20 people</li>\r\n<li>Rose water 1 small bottle</li>\r\n<li>Priest Dakshina</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>If you are planning to provide lunch, Hall will be included for free and temple will provide plates, spoons, etc. Please book hall at least 2 months ahead of time with Panditji.</p>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,29,'2025-02-01 10:44:48','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(76,'Vahana Puja','vahana-puja','15','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">List of Items for Vahana Puja</h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Please contact Panditji and/or Manager to schedule a puja.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Lemon or Lime 4</li>\r\n<li>Coconut 1</li>\r\n<li>Bananas 5</li>\r\n<li>Apples 2</li>\r\n<li>Priest Dakshina</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>This puja is only performed after the regular temple aarti each day.</li>\r\n<li>If it is raining, snowing, or very low temperature we can not perform this puja. Please schedule on a day with good weather.</li>\r\n<li>After the puja, you have to remove/clean coconut and lemon pieces.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30 \">Temple Donation</h3>\r\n<h4>Puja at Temple - $59/-</h4>\r\n<h5>*Priest dakshina separate for both</h5>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,28,'2025-02-01 10:45:23','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(77,'Wedding Anniversary Puja','wedding-anniversary-puja','15','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<h3 class=\"text-primary mt-30\">List of Items for Wedding Anniversary Puja</h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Please contact Panditji and/or Manager to schedule a puja.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Flowers 1 bouquet</li>\r\n<li>Coconut 1</li>\r\n<li>Some fruits</li>\r\n<li>Priest Dakshina</li>\r\n</ol>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,27,'2025-02-01 10:45:56','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(78,'Hall Booking','hall-booking','root','nopage',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,5,'2025-02-03 07:29:45','2025-03-20 23:31:28'),(79,'Change Hall Booking','change-hall-booking','78','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,25,'2025-02-03 07:30:18','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(80,'Cancel Hall Booking','cancel-hall-booking','78','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,26,'2025-02-03 07:31:11','2025-03-20 23:31:29'),(81,'VCN','vcn','28','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Vedanta is one of the world\'s most ancient religious philosophies and one of its broadest. Based on the Vedas, the sacred scriptures of India, Vedanta affirms the oneness of existence, the divinity of the soul, and the harmony of religions. Vedanta is the philosophical foundation of Hinduism; but while Hinduism includes aspects of Indian culture, Vedanta is universal in its application and is equally relevant to all countries, all cultures, and all religious backgrounds.</p>\r\n<p>A closer look at the word \"Vedanta\" is revealing: \"Vedanta\" is a combination of two words: \"Veda\" which means \"knowledge\" and \"anta\" which means \"the end of\" or \"the goal of.\" In this context the goal of knowledge isn\'t intellectual&mdash;the limited knowledge we acquire by reading books. \"Knowledge\" here means the knowledge of God as well as the knowledge of our own divine nature. Vedanta, then, is the search for Self-knowledge as well as the search for God.</p>\r\n<p>What do we mean when we say God? According to Vedanta, God is infinite existence, infinite consciousness, and infinite bliss. The term for this impersonal, transcendent reality is Brahman, the divine ground of being. Yet Vedanta also maintains that God can be personal as well, assuming human form in every age.</p>\r\n<p>Most importantly, God dwells within our own hearts as the divine Self or Atman. The Atman is never born nor will it ever die. Neither stained by our failings nor affected by the fluctuations of the body or mind, the Atman is not subject to our grief or despair or disease or ignorance. Pure, perfect, free from limitations, the Atman, Vedanta declares, is one with Brahman. The greatest temple of God lies within the human heart.</p>\r\n<p>Vedanta further asserts that the goal of human life is to realize and manifest our divinity. Not only is this possible, it is inevitable. Our real nature is divine; God-realization is our birthright. Sooner or later, we will all manifest our divinity&mdash;either in this or in future lives&mdash;for the greatest truth of our existence is our own divine nature.</p>\r\n<p>Finally, Vedanta affirms that all religions teach the same basic truths about God, the world, and our relationship to one another. Thousands of years ago the Rig Veda declared: \"Truth is one, sages call it by various names.\" The world\'s religions offer varying approaches to God, each one true and valid, each religion offering the world a unique and irreplaceable path to God-realization. The conflicting messages we find among religions are due more to doctrine and dogma than to the reality of spiritual experience. While dissimilarities exist in the external observances of the world religions, the internals bear remarkable similarities.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-start align-items-start\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 mb-30\">\r\n<h6>BRAIN - VEDANTA &amp; YOGA</h6>\r\n<iframe style=\"border: none; overflow: hidden;\" src=\"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2F100014882884304%2Fvideos%2F538042660035159%2F&amp;show_text=0&amp;width=100%\" width=\"100%\" height=\"400\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" sandbox=\"\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 mb-30\">\r\n<h6>Youth Group 2014 Project</h6>\r\n<iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7_V9czVhwDc\" width=\"100%\" height=\"400\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12\">\r\n<h6>Sanatana Dharma Opening Prayer at&nbsp;Nebraska State Legislative Assembly</h6>\r\n<iframe style=\"border: none; overflow: hidden;\" src=\"https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FHinduTemple.Omaha.Nebraska%2Fvideos%2F479106706375333%2F&amp;show_text=0\" width=\"100%\" height=\"400\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" sandbox=\"\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe></div>\r\n</div>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,74,'2025-02-07 05:22:55','2025-03-20 23:22:42'),(82,'Book Now','book-now','78','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,9,'2025-02-19 10:07:52','2025-03-20 23:31:28'),(83,'About Sant sadan','about-sant-sadan','28','pageview',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\"><img class=\"w-100\" src=\"https://admin.htom.us/images/media/Untitled-design-(3)_2bgrkwdkr.webp\" alt=\"\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-9\">\r\n<h2 class=\"text-primary mb-15\">About Sant Sadan</h2>\r\nWe have built a Sant Sadan (Hall of Saints) in the Community Center of our Hindu Temple at Omaha, Nebraska, USA. The idea is to celebrate the lives of our prominent saints and Maharishis, this will serve to educate our next generations of Indian Americans about these saints and their contributions to Sanatana Dharma(Hinduism). The Sant Sadan will be the home of the spiritual and vedantic part of our beloved Hindu Temple. It will also be a Center of Learning for the Santana Dharma in North America. We plan to invite prominent religious leaders, yogis, academics and other prominent speakers to come to the Sant Sadan to share their Gyana (knowledge) with us. It is a major initiative for the future generations of our Hindu community in North America. The Sant Sadan is a place to visit with your children, to teach them about our great saints and their contributions. We have chosen 12 saints to start with, we hope to keep adding to this endeavor as we have numerous great saints in the Sanatana Dharma. It includes female saints, as in the Sanatana Dharma there have been numerous female saints that are revered by the Hindus. In fact there were more than 30 female rishis who contributed to the Rigveda alone.</div>\r\n</div>','[]',1,0,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,8,'2025-03-12 23:25:53','2025-06-24 01:33:23');
